### What Problem This Solves

When the Session Reaper encounters a persistence error (EACCES, disk full, etc.) during `sweepCronRunSessions`, the throttle timestamp (`lastSweepAtMsByStore`) is never updated, causing the next timer tick to immediately retry the sweep. This creates an unbounded retry loop with severe CPU and disk I/O thrashing until the underlying condition resolves.

### Why This Change Was Made

The catch block at `session-reaper.ts:125` logged the error and returned early without calling `lastSweepAtMsByStore.set(storePath, now)`. The min-interval throttle check relies on this timestamp to enforce the 5-minute cooldown (`MIN_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS`). Without the update, every subsequent tick passes the throttle guard and retries the failing operation.

### What Changed

Added `lastSweepAtMsByStore.set(storePath, now)` in the catch block (1 line) before returning, so the reaper respects the cooldown period even after a failure.

### User Impact

- No more unbounded retry loops during transient disk/permission errors
- Reduces CPU and disk I/O on systems with temporary filesystem issues
- Session Reaper correctly backs off and retries at the standard 5-minute interval

### Evidence

#### Verification Environment
- Linux / Node.js v22.19.0

#### Verification Method
Wrote a behavior verification test mocking `listSessionEntries` to throw an error (simulating EACCES):

1. First call (force=true) → error caught by catch block, returns `{swept: false, pruned: 0}`
2. Second call 1ms later (force=false, default throttle behavior) → checks throttle
   - Before fix: throttle never updated → retries immediately (infinite loop)
   - After fix: throttle updated in catch block → blocked by `MIN_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS` → returns `{swept: false}`

#### Results
- ✅ Error path now updates throttle timestamp, subsequent call is throttled
- ✅ Existing test suite: 19/19 passed

#### Before
```ts
// catch block returned without updating throttle
try {
  // ...
} catch (err) {
  params.log.warn(...);
  return { swept: false, pruned: 0 };
}
// lastSweepAtMsByStore — never set on error
```

#### After
```ts
try {
  // ...
} catch (err) {
  params.log.warn(...);
  lastSweepAtMsByStore.set(storePath, now);  // <-- 1 line added
  return { swept: false, pruned: 0 };
}
```

Fixes #105188
